      "path": "stellar-forge/mcp-merchant-operator/providers/fred-workspaces.mjs",
      "content": "// MIT. Original FRED workspace metadata and lazy native owner hooks.\nimport { defineMerchantProvider, MERCHANT_PROVIDER_SCHEMA } from '../provider-contract.mjs';\nimport { fredWorkspaceTools } from '../catalog/fred-workspace.mjs';\n\nexport default defineMerchantProvider({\n  schema: MERCHANT_PROVIDER_SCHEMA,\n  id: 'fred-workspaces', family: 'fredWorkspaces',\n  title: 'FRED economic workspaces', order: 0, catalogOrder: 10,\n  configKey: 'fredWorkspaces', summary: true, dependencies: [],\n  concurrency: 'host', concurrentTools: [], shutdown: 'drain',\n  maxRequestBytes: 32 * 1024 * 1024,\n  configuration: {\n    input: 'fredWorkspaceConnection', privateExports: true,\n    read: async (value, { hostPath }) =>\n      (await import('../fred-workspace-client.mjs')).readFredWorkspaceConfiguration(hostPath(value)),\n  },\n  tools: fredWorkspaceTools,\n  load: () => import('../fred-workspace.mjs'),\n  create: (module, config, options) => new module.MerchantFredWorkspaces(config, {\n    environment: options.environment, ...options.fredWorkspaces,\n  }),\n  initialize: async options =>\n    (await import('../fred-workspace-setup.mjs')).initializeFredWorkspaceMerchant(options),\n  instructions: [\n    { prefix: 'merchant_fred_research_', order: 0, text: 'Use the original FRED project Research catalogue, source definitions, retained source reviews and issued products. Follow nextOffset with the same expectedRevision and returned asOf for time-sensitive catalogue/entry/product pages; use separate product and taxonomy pages. Inspect configured research-source and research-catalogue input aliases, bind their complete SHA256, then acquire or upload original files through stable id/revision operations. Review the actual source before ACCEPT; issue products only after explicit source requirements are covered. Inspect the same operation after interruption and resume its retained payload. Download original source bytes, complete catalogue/entry/product records through merchant_fred_file_read; continue its readId/offset to the exact full length. A version7 whole project retains every full source, definition, review and product edition, including existing DDP/QCEW work, and uses the original480MiB receiver.' },\n    {prefix:'merchant_fred_handover',order:2,text:'Move complete customer workspaces through the original retained handover operation. Export at an explicit project revision and capture timestamp with selected publication IDs and an optional configured operating-plan input. Preserve the same operation ID on retry; inspect its active phase and retryAction. Stream configured operating-archive inputs through upload, inspect their complete source graph, receive, then open the original project. Download by exact SHA256 to one new archive filename under the configured private exports directory. Keep complete binary archives in native files and return only retained status/file metadata. Private startup records remain private; QCEW contexts are supplied by the original host. Earlier customer procedure receipts preserve later matching local edits.'},\n    {prefix:'merchant_fred_operating_',order:1,text:'Prepare economic Operating Plans from a complete retained FRED source descriptor and the actual installed catalog. Keep the original project, source basis, compact evidence IDs, stable plan ID and explicit savedAt. Record only the returned evidence belonging to the selected original phase and project continuation. Receive full matching plan history, preserve later local edits, and render complete editable JSON alongside readable HTML or Markdown. These tools use the pure model; capture and whole source receiving are explicit native CLI operations. Original workspace tools retain their 128 KiB request and paged-result behavior.'},\n    {\n      \"prefix\": \"merchant_fred_\",\n      \"text\": \"For economic editions, attach the original FRED workspace and inspect its exact project/launch binding, current revision and declared source/payment profiles. Keep full original public-table text, publisher metadata, series frequencies/units, missing values and API real-time versus public retrieval-date semantics. Import complete host inputs, combine retained captures and save the exact projection review before publication. Follow original observation/comparison offsets and pinned record revisions through complete collections. Prepare each paid dataset page or advertised source file under its original intent; carry the exact returned snapshot and previous-page cursor metadata to the next page. Execute through the configured SF88 buyer and recover the same intent after an interrupted result. Download complete original source, project and customer files with their full SHA256 through retained chunks. Project receiving uses the maintained native receiver; reattach the current private connection record to the same original project after its owner restarts. Borrowed client closure preserves the original workspace owner. Reuse saved analyst definitions through briefing_templates and briefing_template_save. Preview each successor on its exact retained capture, inspect rolling dates, missing coverage and source meaning, then save with the same previewId, note and original project revision. Keep preceding report lineage within the same template. Page comparison rows and inventories through their returned offsets/revisions; full briefing-successor JSON/CSV/HTML and project v3 downloads retain complete original reports and definitions. For release work, acquire or import every original metadata, release-calendar and vintage page using the existing host key binding and exact source selection. Keep publisher release dates, FRED information dates, observation dates and source retrieval times distinct. Save a whole-series or original-template watch, inspect coverage and every selected release-plan section, then save the same previewId and watch/source pair. Preserve late-discovered older vintages and source-update rechecks in their original captured spans. Acquire each selected plan/asOf through release_vintage_capture with a stable original operation; use its resulting observation capture in the original analyst and recurring-report workflow. Page release_captures and release_watches inventories through nextOffset with expectedRevision; kind plans and catchUps expose the complete saved history. Download full release-source or release-plan JSON through retained file reads. Project v4 carries every original source, watch, saved plan and completed acquisition for the maintained native receiver, including series-only watches with empty analyst files. A pending release acquisition resumes its original selection, and a staged release import resumes its original capture ID. For complete current publications, use published_operations and published_operation to open the original retained edition. Start or resume the same saved migration/operation/revision with published_start, follow published_report and published_rows through their original comparison IDs and returned offsets, and transfer every exact listed member or full edition-package.tar.gz with published_file_read. Preserve complete original source inventories, native project identity and all six original comparison statuses. For DDP package migration, inspect complete original crosswalk and package inputs, then import their configured host aliases through ddp_crosswalk_import and ddp_package_import. A source already staged by the same original pending operation resumes with its retained crosswalkId or packageId. Retain the original archive, supporting structure files, CSV layout, Board series IDs, dataset, frequency, units, multiplier, missing markers and original current-published source basis. Page ddp_sources inventories at one project revision; inspect crosswalk rows and package series or observations through every returned nextOffset, using source series IDs for package filters. Preserve an original bookmark and analyst note with the saved plan. Review ambiguous mappings through explicit original-candidate map or exclude decisions and per-series period, exact decimal scale and expected-meaning bindings. Preview every migration plan section and save the same complete input with its returned previewId and revision. Acquire a saved migration through one stable ddp_migration_acquire operation; its original pending acquisition owns every selected native FRED batch and its complete immutable receiving. Inspect receiving meanings, status counts and all changed or unchanged rows with exact series filters. Download ddp-crosswalk, ddp-package and ddp-migration as complete JSON, or ddp-receiving as saved JSON, CSV and offline HTML with their original byte counts and SHA256. Use retained chunks for large files and retain the same readId, source selection, expectedSha256 and nextOffset. Complete v5/v6 project receiving validates every original DDP source, immutable plan, native capture, comparison file and original operation history using the same native graph helper. DDP sources allow 384 MiB complete envelopes, and v5/v6 projects allow 480 MiB; version 1–4 project capacities remain 256 MiB. QCEW-containing projects export v6, while DDP-only projects retain v5. Version 6 retains all four DDP array slots, empty when its original state has no DDP activity. Receive earlier QCEW-only and combined v5 files with their exact original optional-family identity. Retain the original QCEW family whenever present, including every original source, CPI capture, saved county profile and complete report file package; complete receiving validates that same original graph. Reopen a received project through its original private workspace connection. For an explicitly selected historical ALFRED acquisition, pass sourceMode ALFRED_VINTAGE to ddp_migration_acquire. Use a configured alfred-metadata input alias for complete original metadata editions; metadataFileSha256 pins the source file, while metadataSha256 pins canonical editions sorted by series. Retain the same operation ID, revision, migration and staged metadata digest on continuation. Preserve ALFRED_VINTAGE_DATE separately from public retrieval time and API realtime fields. Import complete ALFRED captures as kind capture; their original CSV column, text spans, meaning coverage and metadata editions remain in full v5/v6 projects.\",\n      \"order\": 0\n    }\n  ],\n});\n",
